# Edera zone kernel variant: database.
#
# Databases are syscall/IO/memory heavy. The honest build-time deltas are modest: static
# PREEMPT_NONE (throughput over latency) and NUMA balancing off (a DB manages its own memory
# locality; the balancer's scanning is pure overhead). THP stays at MADVISE (the default),
# which is what Postgres/MySQL want -- 'always' causes allocation-latency spikes. The large
# syscall lever for DBs is CPU-mitigations posture, which is a boot flag (mitigations=off),
# NOT this image -- run-pgbench.sh compares against zone:mitigations=off to show that.
# CONFIG_PREEMPT_DYNAMIC is not set
CONFIG_PREEMPT_NONE=y
# CONFIG_NUMA_BALANCING is not set
